soda_mmqc/data/cache/
soda_mmqc/data/cache/*

# Working output of experiments run from other branches (exp-3 and friends).
# Untracked here and easy to `git add` by accident, since `experiments/` is
# otherwise a tracked tree: builders and committed runs live alongside it.
experiments/results/

# Run output, regenerable and per-machine: `mmqc run` writes predictions
# under data/evaluation/<checklist>/<check>/<model>/<arm>/rep-NN/ and
# `mmqc score` writes analysis.json in the same leaf. Committed runs that a
# paper figure depends on live under `experiments/runs/`, which stays
# tracked on purpose -- see experiments/runs/README.md.
#
# The directory itself is part of the layout -- it is where a production
# benchmark writes -- so ignore its contents and keep the directory. The
# rule has to name the contents rather than the directory: a negation
# cannot rescue a file whose parent directory is excluded.
soda_mmqc/data/evaluation/*
!soda_mmqc/data/evaluation/.gitkeep

# `experiments/runs/` is tracked on purpose, but only for what cannot be
# regenerated. Predictions are committed because they cost money and come
# from a non-deterministic model: run the check again and you get
# different ones. An analysis is neither -- it is a pure function of the
# committed predictions, the committed gold and the committed
# eval-manifest.json, so the repo already pins it by pinning those three,
# and `mmqc score` reproduces it for free.
#
# It is also bulky, and by more than it looks: each record embeds a copy of
# expected_output and model_output that both already exist elsewhere in the
# tree, and one analysis covers a whole leaf. Measured on exp-01, the 66
# analyses come to 86 MB against 6 MB of predictions.
experiments/runs/**/analysis.json

# The per-session debug sidecars go too, with one exception.
# `load_predictions` globs prediction.json and ignores everything beside
# it, so tool_audit.json and skill_set.json answer "why did this session
# do that", which is a question for the machine that ran it. They are
# most of the 13 MB the sidecars came to in exp-01, against the
# predictions' 6 MB -- twice the cost of the thing they annotate.
#
# skill_trace.json is the exception: it is a result, not a debug aid.
# exp-02's endpoint 0 reads it to say whether delegation happened at all,
# and like a prediction it comes from the model and cannot be recomputed.
# Ignore the directory's contents rather than the directory, because git
# cannot re-include a file inside a directory it has excluded.
experiments/runs/**/intermediates/*
!experiments/runs/**/intermediates/skill_trace.json

# exp-03 makes tool_audit.json a result too, for its runs only: its cost and
# time endpoint reads `usage` -- cost, turns, duration, tokens -- from it, and
# like the trace that comes from the session and cannot be recomputed. About
# 3 KB a session, 5 MB over exp-03's 1,520.
!experiments/runs/exp-03-checklist-entry/**/intermediates/tool_audit.json

# exp-02 pilot output: 30 sessions used to check that delegation fires at all.
# Its numbers are recorded in thinking/experiments/exp-02-delegation-depth.md;
# the sessions themselves are not experiment data and are not committed.
experiments/runs/exp-02-delegation-depth/smoke/

# exp-03 smoke test: 24 sessions used to check that D dispatches at all.
# Its numbers are recorded in thinking/experiments/exp-03-checklist-entry.md;
# the sessions themselves are not experiment data and are not committed.
experiments/runs/exp-03-checklist-entry/smoke/
